# The Bootstrap 5 JavaScript API 💻

Every Bootstrap component can be instantiated, opened, and closed programmatically with pure JavaScript.

```javascript_not
// 1. Get or create Modal instance
const modalElement = document.getElementById('myModal');
const myModal = new bootstrap.Modal(modalElement, {
  backdrop: 'static',
  keyboard: false
});

// Show modal programmatically (e.g. after async fetch)
myModal.show();

// Hide modal
setTimeout(() => {
  myModal.hide();
}, 3000);
```

# Component Lifecycle Events 📡

All Bootstrap components emit custom events during their lifecycle that you can hook into:

```javascript_not
const myModalEl = document.getElementById('myModal');

// Fired immediately when show() is called:
myModalEl.addEventListener('show.bs.modal', event => {
  console.log('Modal is starting to show!');
});

// Fired when modal has finished transition and is fully visible:
myModalEl.addEventListener('shown.bs.modal', event => {
  document.getElementById('inputEmail').focus();
});

// Fired when modal is hidden:
myModalEl.addEventListener('hidden.bs.modal', event => {
  console.log('Modal closed');
});
```
